# SPEC — pheno-cargo-template

## Purpose
Canonical Rust crate template for the Phenotype monorepo. Consumed by:
- `cargo-generate` (manual): `cargo generate --git https://github.com/KooshaPari/pheno-cargo-template`
- `pheno-scaffold-kit` (programmatic): generates a new crate from this template

## Public API

### `crate_name`
```rust
pub fn crate_name() -> &'static str { "pheno-cargo-template" }
```
Returns the canonical name of the template crate itself. Used by `pheno-scaffold-kit` to verify a generated crate came from this template.

## What gets generated

When a consumer runs `cargo generate`, the following files are produced:

| File | Source | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `Cargo.toml` | `Cargo.toml` | Standalone crate with empty `[workspace]` table (per ADR-023) |
| `src/lib.rs` | `src/lib.rs` | This file (rename to consumer crate) |
| `tests/lib_test.rs` | (generated) | Single integration test verifying `crate_name()` returns the expected name |
| `README.md` | (generated) | Tier 0 template |
| `AGENTS.md` | (generated) | Tier 0 template |
| `llms.txt` | (generated) | Tier 0 template |
| `WORKLOG.md` | (generated) | Tier 0 template |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | (generated) | Tier 0 template |
| `LICENSE-MIT` | (generated) | Standard MIT |
| `LICENSE-APACHE` | (generated) | Standard Apache-2.0 |
| `deny.toml` | (generated) | ADR-023 Rule 3.1 cargo-deny config |
| `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | (generated) | test + audit + deny + coverage |

## Design decisions
- **No async runtime** — pure synchronous template
- **Empty `[workspace]` table** — keeps the generated crate standalone (not part of the root monorepo workspace; per ADR-023)
- **`#![deny(missing_docs)]` is OFF in template** — generated code may want to remove it
- **MIT OR Apache-2.0** — dual license, same as the rest of the fleet
- **Tier 0** — every generated crate is Tier 0 with required meta-bundle

## Versioning
- `0.1.0` — initial release (2026-06-18)
- Backward-compatible; new template variables may be added but defaults preserve behavior
